Z||000000||gkozlov||06-03-2001||08:12 PM||||I have an 87 GT with a five speed. I need to find out what type of tansmissions were available? Isuzu or Muncie. The selector cable is shot and I am only able to get the car into 3rd or 4th gear. I need to know what transmission I have so I can order the correct cable.  Thanks in advance.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A><BR>MSN MESSENGER: wkozlov@hotmail.com<BR>ICQ # 18515452||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||06-03-2001||08:17 PM||||I don't thing any of the V6s had Isuzu trannys, except the 4 speeds. <BR>I have heard other people say Muncie, but I thought all the V6 5sp'd were Getrag. <P>Anyone know for sure?<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-03-2001||08:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B>I don't thing any of the V6s had Isuzu trannys, except the 4 speeds. <BR>I have heard other people say Muncie, but I thought all the V6 5sp'd were Getrag. <P>Anyone know for sure?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>1984, 1985, and 1986 4-spd's are Muncie's<BR>1985 thru 1988 4-cyl 5-spd's are the Isuzu's<BR>Late 1986 thru 1988 V-6's are Muncie Getrag's.<P>There was no such thing as an Isuzu 4-spd in a Fiero.<BR>So the 87 GT has a Muncie Getrag.<P>||||reg||1
